Not in my experience.   With the magic whistle method, you often have to
blow more than once to get the pet outside/inside the shop, you have to
wait until he feels like picking it up, etc...  Whenever I train my pet,
he always grabs an object immediately bringing it to me (sometimes he
drops is one square away, then picks it back up and brings it to me),
then goes back for the next item.  This clears out small shops in
absolutely no time at all.  The only problem is with large shops, and 
then I usually just walk around towards the back once, and the dog will
grab most of the items and bring them up front.
